{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1549630-monkey-business","id":1549630,"title":"Monkey Business","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-03-29T02:09:25-07:00","id":1549630,"title":"Monkey Business","content":"So since the there's an uptick of Fera related content in this forum I would like to share a write-up for a possible backstory for a Gaian Yeren I found on Tumblr:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/pardy-dardy/771680095145476096?source=share\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://64.media.tumblr.com/631d79dcdd1e120422c83e6895fb2778/96c5369bff96bdcd-2e/s250x400/f7eb49c6bdbf2fe6fed1675217c549fceb1a780d.pnj\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/pardy-dardy/771680095145476096?source=share\" target=\"_blank\"> Post by @pardy-dardy &middot; 1 image </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/pardy-dardy/771680095145476096?source=share\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.tumblr.com/pardy-dardy/771680095145476096?source=share </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> \ud83d\udcac 0&nbsp;&nbsp;\ud83d\udd01 11&nbsp;&nbsp;\u2764\ufe0f 15&nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;BtWoD: The Great Monkeying&nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;had a fucking brain blast earlier about the Yeren and their place in the broader mythology and did a funky in-world piece about it. figured they need&hellip; </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But, there were species of Were-Ape that existed, and that I\u2019m pretty sure are still around. You might know them by the name \u201cYeren\u201d or something. Their symbol looked a bit.... like.... this.<br /> <br /> <img title=\"image.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_1820_1743231692812_325\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1820\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1820\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1820&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"image.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> Yeah, the ones that Pentex claims they invented. No, they didn\u2019t <i>invent a Shifter</i>. The Wyrm can\u2019t invent anything, didn\u2019t you pay attention when your Elders were giving you lessons on the Triat, kids? Fuck. Where was I?<br /> <br /> Yeah, the Yeren. They loved to push the boundaries, inventing crazy shit and diving deep into the Umbra with the best of us. </div> </div> </div>So according to the post above the Yeren are basically the &quot;scientists&quot; of the Fera, well before the concept of science was conceived. Delving into mysteries of Gaia both physical and spiritual, so they could find new ways for both them and the rest of the Fera to preserve and serve Gaia.<br /> <br /> I'd Imagine that Yeren discovered and/or invented many things during they time on Gaia, such say <a href=\"https://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2009/12/091222105312.htm\" target=\"_blank\">fire</a>, new spirits and ways to talk to them, many rites that are adapted and refined by other Fera and of course they more famous invention, the warfrom or as the garou called it the Crinos.<br /> <br /> Yes you head right the Yeren was the inventor of the warfrom and technically the humanoid form because turns out the Fera didn't start out part human.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But hey, you wanna know a secret? I heard this one from a Mokole-Mbembe I\u2019m pals with down in The Big Easy, he said it really changed his perspective on things. Lemme finish this glass real quick and I\u2019ll regale you. I\u2019ve got all night.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Listen up kids, \u2018cause I\u2019m about to tell you about <i>The Great Monkeying</i>. Back before the Impergium, a long, long time ago\u2014 S<b>hifters didn\u2019t have Homid forms. Didn\u2019t have Half-Homid forms neither. Makes sense, doesn\u2019t it? We were just <i>animals</i> that could get bigger and smarter and tougher when we needed. There were outliers who could take weird-ass forms like the Dragon Kings could, but as far as we know, they didn\u2019t look like Humans.</b><br /> <br /> Have you ever wondered why we Fera can <i>all turn into a single type of ape</i>? It\u2019s not like Homo Sapiens ain\u2019t a fuckin species of animal too. It\u2019s basic biology shit. </div> </div> </div>So yes before an event known as <i>&quot;The Great Monkeying&quot;</i> all the Fera (beside the Dragon Kings because they're weird like that) didn't have any other form rather than they're default animal form and Hipaso or equvilant, no Humanoid and definably not Crinos.<br /> <br /> Now how could a singe species of Fera could irreversibly change the spiritual make up of all the fera that currently and will exist so they can shape shift into new form? Weill it's a matter of simply finding the right patron and willingness to make the necessary sacrifices.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They got approached by a powerful Spirit at some point who made them an offer they couldn\u2019t pass up. It would teach them a powerful ritual that would grant their fellow Fera brand new forms to use in the fight against the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> Imagine that! Granting every Fera that currently exists and will exist the capability to use <i>entirely new forms</i>?? The offer was too good to refuse obviously, and they entered a relationship with this new Patron. Time went on, and since nobody was really paying attention to them, they got to finishing their Ritual without a hitch.<br /> <br /> Of course, the final step was to sacrifice themselves. Yeah, everyone. All at once. Hey, listen here. You might not think that it\u2019d be a good idea, but these fuckin apes were crazy. They knew they\u2019d die, but they also knew that they\u2019d have committed such an incredible sacrifice that they\u2019d live on forever. And, well. They kinda succeeded, just not in the way they might\u2019ve wanted.<br /> \u200b </div> </div> </div>So yes if you want grant all the Fera that has and Will Exist the ability to turn in to giant Murder Furries all you need to get the patronage of a powerful sprit (which was revealed to be an aspect of the weaver) and convince you're whole tribe to sacrifice themselves (because yes the Yeren are divided into tribes and the humanoids (think Homo sapiens, Erectus, Neanderthals, ect) being the ones primary responsible for this mess) in a event known as the (aforementioned) Great Monkeying.<br /> <br /> Now a ritual as grand and far-reaching as this must have left some spiritual fallout and well...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Here\u2019s another thing you gotta realize too, kids. There were no mages or whatever before Humanity got its footing. There just <i>weren\u2019t</i>. Not the way we know them. You can blame the monkeys for them showing up though, \u2018cause their sacrifice essentially irradiated the earth around their Kinfolk with so much Gnosis that a bunch of them turned into the first mages.<br /> <br /> And you know how mages can shape reality to whatever the hell their twisted perception is? It should be obvious by now where this is going. </div> </div> </div>Yeah turns out the Humanoid Yeren accidentally created the Mages. And like proper mages they proceed to mess things up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> These new mages saw themselves reflected in the Fera. Anthropomorphized them and shit. Like if steamboat willie were a cave painting. They applied Human characteristics to the Shifters, and as a result, they <i>literally made them Human.</i> One by one, as mythologies about men who turned into beasts and back spread across the earth, the Fera suddenly found themselves <i>Human</i>, in addition to being whatever animal they are. </div> </div> </div>So essentially the new mages saw the confused humanoid fera stumbling around and decide to apply human characteristics to them which thanks to the simple fact they're mages and consensus reality is near nonexistent at the time promptly turned all the Freas into part humans and not merly animals that can shapeshift into humans. And the Feras took that fact reeely well /sarcasum.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Okay, so. Everyone\u2019s obviously pissed that they suddenly can turn into naked apes. It\u2019s a violation of just about every conception of consent out there. Everyone turns to the Homen to turn them to mush\u2014 wait, shit. I forgot something. The Yeren had a couple Tribes, and the one that did all this shit were Clan Homen. Homo sapiens. The gorillas and orangutans didn\u2019t have shit to do with it. Anyways, the spiders tell everyone that Clan Homen had been working with an extension of the Weaver directly, and that they probably\u2019d been tricked.<br /> <br /> That didn\u2019t do shit to make anyone less angry. They wanted blood, and even more so after not even the greatest mystics around couldn\u2019t figure out how to undo it. So, the Fera decided to turn on the other Yeren\u2014 just a little too late, though. About 99% of the bastards had fled deep into the Umbra before retribution could come \u2018round, and we only <i>rarely</i> see them these days.<br /> \u200b </div> </div> </div>So yeah the Fera went on a warpath intent on punshinging the perpetrators of from they view an unimaginable breach of the natural order and if there's colltral damage so be it. The whole thing will be remembered by the future generations as the Impergium.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Yeren flee into the Umbra, the Fera are pissed off, yadda yadda everyone\u2019s fighting and upset. Actually, the story is basically over. Oh yeah, and this is what started the Impergium by the way. We got too heated about Humanity so we decided to start killing them. Look where that got us! Ugh. God, I\u2019m too drunk to have fun right now. Lets get something to eat, I need to sober up. </div> </div> </div>Of course you're free to take the whole thing with a mound of salt since the person telling the story is a very drunk Nuwisha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-31T08:17:13-07:00","id":1549668,"title":"","content":"The funny thing is according the 2003 Players Guide to the Changing Breeds there are rumours among the Beast Courts of breeds of sapient shapeshifting orangutans in the Indonesian rainforests","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-31T14:21:07-07:00","id":1549678,"title":"","content":"Those go back to the 1e core, even.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-31T14:46:49-07:00","id":1549683,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d argue that ape-changers or monkey-changers would be less interesting than a \u2018missing link\u2019 type species, if only because turning from a human into some other species of primate is rather a lateral move (Since it lacks the inherent Cool factor of becoming a creature with strengths completely unlike our own and a very different experience of this world).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}